# cuts/v1.0.35/cut.env
# ============================================================================
# THE PINS FOR v1.0.35. Read by bin/rollforward_gate.sh --cut v1.0.35 and by
# scripts/verify_cut_pin_is_current.sh.
#
# WHY v1.0.35 EXISTS: v1.0.34 BUILT A PERFECT DMG AND THREW IT AWAY.
#
# This is not a re-cut of a broken build. v1.0.34's artefact was complete and
# correct, and nobody ever had it. Measured on run 32093975602:
#
#     03:10:03  DMG notarised, status: Accepted
#     03:10:03  stapled, "The staple and validate action worked!"
#     03:10:04  spctl, source=Notarized Developer ID
#     03:10:09  publish-appcast: OSTLER_SPARKLE_SIGNING_KEY unset -> Error 1
#               make ship non-zero
#               "Verify the artefact" SKIPPED, upload-artifact SKIPPED
#     actions/runs/32093975602/artifacts -> total_count = 0
#
# Five seconds between a notarised build and an ephemeral runner being torn
# down with the only copy on it. The version number was spent on a defect in
# step ORDERING, not in anything the DMG contained.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WHAT CHANGED IN THE CUT PATH, so this cannot repeat
#
# CM051 #828 (3a0cb120):
#   * `if: always()` on the staging/verify step AND on upload-artifact. The
#     artefact leaves the runner as soon as it exists, before anything
#     downstream is allowed an opinion about it.
#   * publish-appcast lifted OUT of `ship:` and invoked after the upload.
#   * continue-on-error deliberately ABSENT from that step.
#
# THE PUBLISH STEP IS EXPECTED TO END RED ON THIS CUT, AND THAT IS THE DESIGN.
# Measured on this repo, secret NAMES only: OSTLER_SPARKLE_SIGNING_KEY is not
# among the seven Actions secrets. So the hard-require fires, the step fails,
# and the job goes red WITH the DMG already uploaded. A red run that hands back
# a complete artefact is the outcome #828 was built to produce. Do not read it
# as a failed cut, and do not work around it -- the appcast stays a known dark
# surface tracked at #370 until the signing-key question is answered by Andy.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# THE PINS BELOW ARE MEASURED, NOT ASSERTED
#
# Daemon, checked against the published sidecar rather than the Makefile
# comment that names it:
#
#     gui/Makefile   DAEMON_VERSION 0.4.58  DAEMON_SHA256 d4f274cb...
#     install.sh     OSTLER_ASSISTANT_VERSION 0.4.58
#     install.sh     DEFAULT_ASSISTANT_TARBALL_SHA256 d4f274cb...
#     published      hub-v0.4.58 .tar.gz.sha256          d4f274cb...
#
# Wiki images v0.1.18 from CM044 bf5dfe68, digests read from the ghcr registry
# rather than from the PR that claimed them, and bound in
# scripts/wiki_image_provenance.tsv.
#
# vendor:ostler_fda is re-pinned to 9cf567be and carries the #417 calendar
# backfill graft, so check-freshness is GREEN rather than held.
#
# CM051 names main at the time of writing. This branch does NOT touch
# install.sh (measured: 0 install.sh paths in its diff), so the pin and the
# shipping tree agree by CONTENT and not merely by ordering:
#
#     CM051 pin 3a0cb120  install.sh blob  fb49d304d893249f3c7fc3b124cfe51b5a78d1e8
#     origin/main         install.sh blob  fb49d304d893249f3c7fc3b124cfe51b5a78d1e8
#
# RE-VERIFY IMMEDIATELY BEFORE PUSHING THE TAG, AFTER THE LAST MERGE, NOT
# BEFORE IT:
#
#     git rev-parse $CM051:install.sh
#     git rev-parse origin/main:install.sh
#
# If they diverge, re-point CM051 to main and re-run. A pin chosen early and
# trusted is what burnt v1.0.31.
# ============================================================================

# The daemon. hub-v0.4.58, signed, notarised and stapled. Unchanged from
# v1.0.33 and v1.0.34 -- this cut rebuilds no daemon. DEREFERENCED commit: the
# tag is ANNOTATED and its tag object is 87cd9d9e, and recording that would pin
# the cut to a tag object rather than to source.
DAEMON_COMMIT=5b7efb00a541

# The CM051 tree whose install.sh ships in the DMG. See the blob note above.
CM051=3a0cb12068e7c2f6c201f575782de1f09d20658a
